From 35044ec8fa7acd166154cd034d1950924073aa0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:52:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Use SQLite-only wallet storage for the V2 development series

Create wallet.sqlite directories with LV2W schema version 1 and an exact caller-supplied storage profile. Reject wallet.dat, individual database paths, foreign SQLite files and mismatched profiles without conversion. The inherited RPC/tool adapter uses an explicit development storage marker; it is not V2 chain identity or V2 transaction/signing integration.

Remove BerkeleyDB source, discovery, dependency packaging and salvage. Complete SQLite mock, transaction ownership, discovery, backup, restore and secure-deletion behavior. Validate native database transactions/reopen/backup/rejection plus all inherited wallet suites and isolated inherited ABC regtest encryption/backup/restore RPC round trips.
